WEBVTT

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:01.880
<i>Yummy!</i>

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:06.140
Today's lunch special
tastes fairly unique.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.930
That was so delicious.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.640
At first I thought they must've been
joking with the roasted pickles.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.150
Um, by the way...

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.440
Nao, why are you staring at me?

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.780
No reason.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.660
How about a nice after-lunch refreshment?

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.910
Oh! The <i>Joie</i> Lady!
What great timing.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.170
Which <i>Joie</i> flavor should I choose today?

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.540
You took the fermented milk one before.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.260
The only flavor approved as food for
specified health uses is plain.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.930
W-What the hell?

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.980
-Oh, it's the "Kingdom" guy.
-Huh?

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.400
W-What?

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.860
A mass proposal?

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.620
It is an honor to meet you.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.160
Sada Hinomoto.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.410
Huh?

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.190
Let me introduce you

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.440
the former Vice Minister from
the Imperial Household Agency

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.690
and ceremony official, Mr. Iboshi.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.820
A very prestigious man!

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.950
He's not the "Kingdom" guy.
He's an imperialist.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.740
What's is he doing Gifu?

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.580
The moment we've been waiting,
has arrived.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.290
You, the White Lovers, will finally learn
your true mission...

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:26.050
with the Organic Transformed Fliers.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.340
White Lovers?

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:30.880
The true mission.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:36.850
Seventy-four years ago, the country put
all its effort into a great Ritual...

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.850
the execution of The Rule.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:40.770
The Rule?

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:47.730
Organic Transformed Fliers are terrifying
if misused and can cause great damage.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.610
And so there is one
to rule over them all...

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.110
and that is Lord Mitatsu.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.780
Every 74 years, Lord Mitatsu awakens...

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.910
to be transported to
its next place of rest,

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.080
Fushido.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:05.130
Guiding Lord Mitatsu,
so that he does not get lost...

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:12.220
is the true duty of the White Lovers
and the Organic Transformed Fliers.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.890
So? Do you understand?

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.270
I didn't understand a thing.
It was so sudden, I'm totally lost.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.980
I wonder if this Lord Mitatsu
is bigger than Futomomo.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.520
To deal with unforeseen circumstances,

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:32.490
we have a combined task force comprised of
all three Self-Defense Force branches.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:37.120
The deserted island training was part
of a larger military operation.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:43.120
That island itself was actually
the sleeping Lord Mitatsu.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.120
Huh?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.210
And the ones to rouse
Lord Mitatsu from his slumber

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:50.710
were you, the White Lovers.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.800
What?

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:56.930
With all self-defense forces mobilized,
your mission as Dragon Pilots...

00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:01.600
will be to guide the large-scale OTF
to its new throne.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:07.730
The Rule will tentatively be called,
The Gifu Mixed Formation Operation.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.230
But, the mixed formation
would be limited.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.650
So the heat dispersion flights
were nothing but masquerades?

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.160
It is true that the OTF
still needs to release heat.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.580
They were not completely pointless.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:23.330
At least it was worth
getting all sweaty every day.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:28.330
This is not some pipe dream.
It is and unmistakably reality...

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:32.340
and a proper mission for us to fulfill.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:34.300
Bear that in mind.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.770
Somehow, I still can't believe it.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:48.270
Although, I guess I'm not the one to talk,
especially while I'm inside Masotan.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:54.280
Still, we'll do an extra careful check,
since the real training starts tomorrow.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:55.780
Um...

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.320
<i>Gear down.</i>

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:02.620
<i>Okonogi, weren't you surprised , huh?</i>

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:07.000
I was surprised. But there are
things that need to be done.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.460
<i>You're so positive.</i>

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:10.500
<i>Ailerons.</i>

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:12.800
Right. Left.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:16.970
<i>Air brake, open.</i>

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:18.880
<i>Open.</i>

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:20.390
<i>Close.</i>

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:21.930
Next.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.850
<i>-Nozzle, right.</i>
-Nozzle, right.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:30.560
<i>We are tuned up!</i>

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:32.690
Check completely.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.190
<i>Got it. I'll  check completely!</i>

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:37.690
Oh, that's right!

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.570
-<i>Okonogi!</i>
-Yes?

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.570
Huh?

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:46.290
Here I am!

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.910
Did you get it?

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.170
It's a sound from the zombie movie
to signal when I want out of Masotan!

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.840
-Remember this?
-Oh, I get it.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.470
You know what?
We were watching a remake!

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.470
The original is now on Blu-ray
or something!

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:05.220
Is that so?

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:09.730
I'll order it online so we can watch
how crappy it is over and over together!

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.940
But I guess we can't watch it
by ourselves in the barracks.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.820
T-Those two...

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.820
After one date,
how far are they taking it?

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:24.370
This place is packed.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.040
But why is everyone gathered here?

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:29.580
Our guest is here.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:00.570
The... <i>Joie</i> Lady?

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.910
Not going to stand for me?

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.530
Oh! A...

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.280
Attention!

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:07.780
Bow!

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:09.790
Good morning!

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:11.660
Huh?

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.790
Yes, good morning.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:15.880
Be seated!

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.550
The woman standing before you

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:24.760
took to the skies during the Pacific War
with an OTF 74 years ago.

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:26.680
A genuine White Lover.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.140
In other words...

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:34.140
She is the last living Dragon Pilot
with experience of previous missions.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.650
What?

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:41.400
Which means that she's Nao's mom and
Moriyama's senior's senior's senior!

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:44.660
Well, we also learned
of this only yesterday.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:48.450
Ms. Hinomoto was chosen
to be a Dragon Pilot...

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:51.160
and assigned to the army aviation unit
in complete secrecy.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:56.540
In Rabaul, Papua New Guinea,
she saved many of her comrades.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:01.920
And before we knew it, she was being
called the Heavenly Maiden of Rabaul.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:05.430
No wonder our bodies
moved so fast for her.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:07.930
Jeez! She made me nervous.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.680
About The Rule...

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:16.940
safely delivering Lord Mitatsu
to his destination...

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:19.020
will not be a walk in the park.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:23.360
I used to think, being an escort
would've been easy.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.650
I wonder if he's impatient.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:29.950
No, Lord Mitatsu moves
at a very slow pace.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:32.870
Slowly, slowly.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:37.920
It will take three days and three nights
at that pace to reach the destination.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.750
-Huh?
-No way...

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:43.010
That's right. For three days and nights...

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:46.430
you must fly the whole time.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:51.680
<i>Hiso Maso!</i>

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:52.640
<i>Woo!</i>

00:09:58.310 --> 00:09:59.150
El!

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:02.440
Uh, I meant Hoshino.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:03.980
Well...

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:08.240
since we can't fly for three days
straight with you...

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:11.740
we'll be following you in shifts
as much as we can.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:12.700
Thanks.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:15.790
All right. See you later.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.220
<i>I never would've guessed</i>
<i>the Joie Lady...</i>

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.680
<i>is actually Ms. Sada, a Dragon Pilot</i>
<i>from way back.</i>

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:37.100
I was just as surprised.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.850
It was a big surprise, but...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.270
The operation will take place
in three months' time.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:44.320
So soon!

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:48.990
Until then, Ms. Hinomoto will be
guiding you with her experience.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:51.370
Excuse me!

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:54.370
What if we fall asleep
in the middle of it?

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:58.290
Lord Mitatsu will lose
sight of his path...

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:02.330
and wreak havoc on wherever he ends up.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:08.800
Is it even possible for Norma and
others to fly for three days straight?p

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:11.680
The OTF does not require replenishment.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:14.810
Everything depends on the Dragon Pilots.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.220
That's impossible...

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:20.020
Did you really not sleep?

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:24.230
Of course I couldn't stay awake.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:25.480
Then?

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:29.070
You just have to fly in your dreams.

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:31.320
In our dreams?

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.450
As long as you don't lose your path...

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:39.750
your OTF will always fly with you.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.090
<i>Why can humans stock up food</i>
<i>but not sleep?</i>

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:49.210
Masotan can take over for short distances.

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:51.340
Don't get so worked up about it.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:52.930
Wow.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:55.600
-Are they reading each other's minds?
-Wrong!

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.720
I signaled for the left aileron!

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:01.020
Gosh, I don't understand this crap at all!

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:02.730
-Or maybe not.
-Or maybe not.

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.910
Don't knock out everyone.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.590
The Maritime Self-Defense
Force target tug...

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:37.510
has arrived at 20,000 feet.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.890
It's being towed at 20 knots per hour.

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:44.440
They've entered the golf course airspace.

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.480
All aircraft commence operation.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:48.400
FIRST DAY... 6:00 A.M. J.S.T.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.530
<i>Awesome.</i>

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:03.410
<i>If this were a fight, the enemy</i>
<i>wouldn't know what's coming from behind.</i>

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:06.790
<i>Only VTOL move at that speed.</i>

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:15.590
We're moving so slow,
I feel like I'm pedaling a bike.

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.680
<i>"Do not fly off alone...</i>

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:20.100
<i>fly with them."</i>

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.720
<i>It's Ms. Hinomoto instructions.</i>

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.100
<i>The Joie Lady?</i>

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:30.110
<i>I meant to say, Ms. Sada!</i>

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:32.690
Roger!

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:36.490
Sustaining a hovering position
at low speed for three days...

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:38.950
That could make a person faint.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:43.450
Lord Mitatsu's speed and traits
are equal to that of a typhoon.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.330
While proceeding at
18 to 24 miles per hour,

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:49.250
it's like trying to stay
in the eye of the storm.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:51.550
Without the OTF,

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:56.170
it would be impossible to follow
Lord Mitatsu so closely.

00:13:56.680 --> 00:14:00.350
FIRST DAY... 6:00 P.M. J.S.T.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:06.560
The pursuit planes are rotating, huh?

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:09.060
SECOND DAY... 6:00 A.M. J.S.T.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:11.270
We've made it past the first hurdle.

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:13.530
Just two more times.

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:16.610
This is as hard as I thought.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:18.990
I'm so sleepy.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:22.950
If I wanted to, I could
fall asleep in a second.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.330
<i>Go ahead.</i>

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:25.370
Huh?

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:30.460
<i>"Convey to the OTF</i>
<i>to take over while you sleep."</i>

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.670
<i>Ms. Hinomoto's instructions.</i>

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.170
I know she says that, but...

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:40.010
That's what it means to fly together.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:42.680
"That's what it means to fly together,"

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:44.600
<i>says Ms. Hinomoto.</i>

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:48.730
SECOND DAY... 11:00 P.M. J.S.T.

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:50.100
Yo.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:52.110
How are they doing?

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.480
It looks considerably difficult.

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:57.190
But they are quite persistent.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:59.650
Anyway, I'll leave it to you.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:00.860
You got it.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.870
THIRD DAY... 3:00 A.M. J.S.T.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:03.830
Hey!

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.080
This does not look good.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:11.580
<i>Hoshino! All of you!</i>

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:14.250
<i>-Keep it together!</i>
-Damn it!

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.760
I don't know...

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:19.930
Am I awake? Am I asleep?

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:22.510
I just don't know anymore.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:42.610
3:00 P.M. J.S.T.

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:55.170
The wire is stretching.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:58.340
-Go to battle speed two!
-Battle speed two!

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:00.720
Keep it at 150 degrees!

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.090
Holding at 150 degrees!

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:07.060
The destroyer is matching
our bearing and speed, but...

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:10.980
Technical Sergeant Hitomi!
Wake up your OTF now!

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:14.230
Flight Leader Kakiyasu.

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:17.270
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.940
9:00 P.M. J.S.T.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:22.240
Snooze...

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.450
Wait for me...

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:29.290
Masotan.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.580
I'll switch with you soon.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.710
Actually, just a little more...

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:41.170
I need...

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.340
to fly...

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:48.720
<i>What the hell are you doing?</i>
<i>You bunch of wimps!</i>

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:53.100
<i>You're all warm and comfy inside,</i>
<i>and you're not even injured!</i>

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.810
<i>You can't even fly for three days?</i>

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:57.480
Ms. Sada...

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:02.110
<i>The fact that you can't sleep...</i>

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:06.990
<i>is the same as not relying on</i>
<i>your Organic Transformed Fliers!</i>

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:10.540
<i>Become one with them and fly!</i>

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:14.250
Why can't you do this spectacular thing?

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:16.750
Knock it off, you fools!!

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:19.040
She just called us fools.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:23.050
<i>The Joie Lady is nowhere to be seen.</i>

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:26.260
If you're not going
to trust your partner fully,

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:28.850
then go fly home now!

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:31.100
<i>I can't be so irresponsible!</i>

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.350
<i>Technical Sergeant Amakasu?</i>

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.520
<i>To put everything on Masotan...</i>

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:37.850
<i>to make only Masotan fly...</i>

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:40.520
<i>to just be sleeping like a baby...</i>

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:42.570
<i>I can't be so unjust!</i>

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:46.400
Don't you get it?
I told you to fly in your dreams!

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:48.240
Yes! That's exactly it!

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:50.620
<i>Ever since meeting Masotan...</i>

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:54.950
I've been able to have the dream of
working hard as a Dragon Pilot.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:57.710
With Masotan...

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:00.250
I've always been flying in a dream!

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.550
<i>She's not talking about</i>
<i>that kind of dream.</i>

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:06.300
<i>So I'm telling you, it's not that</i>
<i>I don't trust Masotan!</i>

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:09.140
<i>I just don't want to be selfish!</i>

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.640
Technical Sergeant Amakasu.

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:12.560
That's why...

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.060
That's why...

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.940
<i>Listen well...</i>
<i>Technical Sergeant Amakasu.</i>

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.190
I'm... still listening... to you.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:25.820
<i>Not to my voice.</i>

00:18:26.110 --> 00:18:28.150
<i>To your Organic Transformed Flier's voice.</i>

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:30.870
Masotan's?

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:37.080
Ah, don't do that, Masotan.

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:41.500
It's like your rhythmic tummy sounds
are welcoming me to sleep.

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.340
<i>Yes, it's telling you to sleep.</i>

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:51.260
<i>All of your thoughts are being</i>
<i>properly conveyed to your OTF.</i>

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:56.640
<i>That's why you, too,</i>
<i>should accept their thoughts.</i>

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.890
Accept... their thoughts...

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:02.610
You want us to sleep...

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:05.980
Masotan... are you sure it's okay?

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:10.990
Thank you, Masotan.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:15.950
I have a good grip
over your thoughts now.

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:28.550
The destroyer's speed has decreased.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:29.880
Those girls!

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:34.470
Your scolding must have
revitalized them, Ms. Hinomoto.

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:37.850
Nope. They're sound asleep.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:39.060
Huh?

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:42.480
Now then, shall we head home?

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:59.950
You can do it! Just a little more!

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:15.930
Let's go.

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:17.510
Montparnasse.

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:25.480
Masotan?

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:28.780
Huh?

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:31.240
<i>Very well done.</i>

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:32.820
Ms. Sada?

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:35.490
<i>You made it through three days!</i>

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:37.450
<i>You guys are amazing!</i>

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:41.540
<i>Hoshino, too... job well done.</i>

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.120
What was that?

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:46.960
It was like the dream we saw before.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:49.960
But then, was it...

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:54.930
It was you, wasn't it, Masotan?

00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:01.770
Welcome home, Amakasu.

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:03.730
Oh, thanks.

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:09.320
What're you doing, Amakasu?

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:12.570
Amakasu! You can't sleep here!

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.200
Amakasu!

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:42.680
Civilians?

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:46.140
Oh!

00:21:56.900 --> 00:21:58.160
Natsume.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:21:59.320
Natsume?

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:02.330
Haru, who is this girl?

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:04.620
Haru?

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:06.870
Right on time.

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:11.500
But the plan for these girls
is confidential.

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:13.920
Who are these girls?

00:22:14.300 --> 00:22:17.430
These are the Miko
who will be essential for The Rule.

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:19.260
Miko?

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:22.430
The presence of these girls...

00:22:22.510 --> 00:22:26.520
is just as important as
the Dragon Pilots and OTF.

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:29.100
And your presence as well.

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:30.230
Huh?

00:22:30.940 --> 00:22:33.070
From the Department of Divinities,

00:22:33.150 --> 00:22:35.990
High Steward Haruto Okonogi.

00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:38.990
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:10.870
<i>-I like you.</i>
<i>-No!</i>

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:12.370
<i>Will you go out with me?</i>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:14.330
<i>I really like you.</i>

00:24:30.980 --> 00:24:33.980
<i></i>
